# 2026-01-25 – Project 06 – Nginx on MacBook

## Summary
Today I deployed and validated an Nginx web server on my MacBook Linux environment.

I focused on understanding how Nginx runs as a service, how it interacts with systemd, and how firewall rules affect accessibility.

## What I Learned
- Nginx runs using a master and multiple worker processes
- `systemctl` is the primary way to manage server services
- A service running does not automatically mean it is accessible
- UFW must be explicitly configured to allow web traffic
- `curl` is a reliable way to validate HTTP services

## What Confused Me
Initially, I assumed the firewall was active by default.  
After checking `ufw status`, I realised it must be explicitly enabled.

## Win
Successfully verified a running web server using systemd, firewall rules, and HTTP validation — end-to-end.
